# /etc/sudoers.d/ict-ufw — passwordless `ufw` for the operator-action workflows.
#
# Save to: /etc/sudoers.d/ict-ufw (mode 0440, validated with visudo -c)
# Installed by: scripts/vm_bootstrap.sh · scripts/ops/purge_vm_runner.sh
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE EXISTS SEPARATELY (2026-08-13) ─────────────────────────────
#
# It is the surviving half of `deploy/claude-vm-runner.sudoers`, which granted
# TWO things:
#
#   ubuntu ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/claude-vm-dispatch   ← REMOVED
#   ubuntu ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/ufw                       ← kept, here
#
# The dispatch grant was a passwordless-root path to a wrapper whose ONLY caller
# — the Telegram `/vm` + `/vm_write` command surface — was deleted in PR #1933
# on 2026-05-25. A full-system audit on 2026-08-13 found it still installed on
# the LIVE MONEY VM three months later, with zero call sites anywhere in `src/`
# (`BL-20260813-VM-RUNNER-ZOMBIE-SUDOERS-ROOT-GRANT`). Nothing exercised it, so
# nothing would have noticed if the wrapper had been replaced.
#
# THE SPLIT IS THE POINT. The obvious remediation — delete
# /etc/sudoers.d/claude-vm-runner — would ALSO have removed the `ufw` grant,
# which is live and load-bearing: the `system-actions` / `vm-net-fix` workflows
# use it to reopen dashboard ingress after the VM-local firewall has blocked
# TCP/8001 across a reboot with iptables-persistent rules unsaved (#537 / #542 /
# #545). Losing it would break the auto-recovery for exactly that outage class,
# and it would break it QUIETLY — the next occurrence would just fail to heal.
#
# So `ufw` moves here, under its own name, with its own justification, and the
# dead grant goes. A grant that has to be read twice to know why it exists is
# the shape that let the dispatch line survive three months of reviews.
#
# ── SCOPE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This grants ONE binary. It does NOT grant systemctl, systemd-run, shell, or
# any path under /usr/local/bin. The tiered mutating actions get their sudo from
# /etc/sudoers.d/ict-system-actions, which is a separate file with a separate
# allowlist — see docs/claude/system-actions.md § "VM sudoers setup".

ubuntu ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/ufw
